<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Model Architecture</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LatinX is a modular pipeline composed of three main components.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Grapheme-to-Phoneme (G2P) Model</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide a robust phonetic input representation, we use <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LatPhon</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, a lightweight Transformer-based encoder-decoder model specifically trained for Romance languages and English.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Neural Audio Codec and Vocoder</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ a neural audio codec, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Spectrogram Patch Codec</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, to discretize speech. Its VQ-VAE component <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> transforms mel-spectrograms into a sequence of discrete indices from a codebook of 4096 vectors, using an encoder with a downsampling factor of 4 and a latent dimension of 512. The model is trained with a combination of a reconstruction loss (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> + LPIPS), an adversarial loss using a PatchGAN discriminator, and a vector quantization commitment loss. A HiFi-GAN vocoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> then converts the reconstructed mel-spectrograms back into a high-fidelity waveform.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Autoregressive Generation Model: LatinX</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The core of our system is a 12-layer decoder-only Transformer with 210M parameters, inspired by LLaMA 2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. The architecture features an embedding dimension of 1024, a 4096-dimensional feed-forward network, and 16 attention heads. For efficiency, we incorporate Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> and FlashAttention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The model operates on a fixed context window of 8192 tokens, partitioned into three segments: 256 tokens for the input phonemes, 3968 tokens for the acoustic prompt (from a 3-second voice sample), and 3968 tokens for the autoregressive generation. It is trained to predict the subsequent audio token based on this combined context. On an NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPU with float16 precision, the model achieves an inference speed of approximately 130 tokens per second. Given that our neural codec produces roughly 630 tokens per second of audio, this corresponds to a Real-Time Factor (RTF) of approximately 4.85, making it suitable for offline synthesis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise stated, we use repetition-aware sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> with top-<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}0.7</annotation></semantics></math>, repetition window size <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W{=}240" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W{=}240</annotation></semantics></math> and max repetition <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Training and Optimization</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The LatinX model is trained in three sequential stages (fig. <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 4 Training and Optimization ‣ LATINX: ALIGNING A MULTILINGUAL TTS MODEL WITH DIRECT PREFERENCE OPTIMIZATION" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) using the AdamW optimizer with <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, and a weight decay of 0.01.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05863v1/dpo_training.png" id="S4.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/115;" width="381" height="115" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>The three-stage training pipeline for the LatinX model, progressing from general pre-training to supervised fine-tuning for voice cloning, and concluding with DPO alignment.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Stage 1: Pre-training</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model is first trained for 400,000 steps on the full dataset with a standard cross-entropy loss objective. This stage teaches the model the fundamental mapping from phonemic sequences to corresponding audio codes, without any speaker conditioning. A cosine decay learning rate schedule with warmup was used.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Stage 2: Supervised Fine-tuning</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we fine-tune the model for zero-shot voice cloning over 30,000 steps. The training data consists of triplets <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{audio}_{\text{context}},\text{text},\text{audio}_{\text{target}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>audio</mtext><mtext>context</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>text</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>audio</mtext><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{audio}_{\text{context}},\text{text},\text{audio}_{\text{target}})</annotation></semantics></math> where all audio originates from the same speaker. To construct these triplets, we enforced a minimum cosine similarity of 0.6 between speaker embeddings of any two utterances. This threshold serves a dual purpose: first, it ensures high intra-speaker acoustic consistency for robust voice cloning; second, it allows us to create reliable pseudo-speaker training data from corpus sections that lack explicit speaker labels, thereby maximizing data utilization. This stage adapts the model to preserve vocal characteristics from the audio prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Stage 3: Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)</h3>

<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Objective</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We optimize <em id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Direct Preference Optimization</em> with a fixed reference policy <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (the SFT model, frozen) and inverse temperature <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E1.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center" colspan="2"><math id="S4.E1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\log\sigma\!\big(\beta\,(\Delta_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\big)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\log\sigma\!\big(\beta\,(\Delta_{\theta}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}})\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1a)</span></td></tr><tr id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{+}\!\mid x)-\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{-}\!\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{+}\!\mid x)-\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{-}\!\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E1.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{+}\!\mid x)-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{-}\!\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{+}\!\mid x)-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{-}\!\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We used <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> and mixed mini-batches with gradient accumulation to stabilize updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The final stage aligns the model with desired metrics for intelligibility and voice similarity using DPO. To achieve this, we constructed a preference dataset following a multi-step automated procedure:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Candidate Generation:</span> To simulate a realistic cascaded S2S scenario, transcriptions were first translated using M2M-100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. For each translated text, we generated five distinct audio candidates using the fine-tuned model from Stage 2. All candidates were produced with repetition-aware sampling, using a temperature of 0.7 and top-p of 1.0.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pair Formation and Filtering:</span> From the five candidates for each source text, we created all possible pairs. We then filtered these pairs to ensure a baseline quality, discarding any pair where a candidate had a WER (measured by Whisper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>) higher than 20% or a speaker similarity (from TitaNet embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>) lower than 0.5.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Preference Labeling:</span> We applied a strict Pareto dominance criterion for labeling. A candidate <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> (winner) was marked as preferred over a candidate <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> (loser) if and only if it was superior on both metrics: <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Sim(y_{w})&gt;Sim(y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Sim(y_{w})&gt;Sim(y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WER(y_{w})&lt;WER(y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WER(y_{w})&lt;WER(y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures an unambiguous preference signal.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset Balancing:</span> The final set of preference pairs was sampled to create a balanced training dataset based on language, audio duration, and the speaker’s mean fundamental frequency (F0).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The model was then trained on this final preference dataset for 4,000 steps using the DPO loss function, refining its policy to maximize the likelihood of generating outputs that are both highly intelligible and faithful to the source voice.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Detailed Word Error Rate (WER %) by source and target language. Best results per row in bold.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:103.7pt;vertical-align:-50.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-210.8pt,63.4pt) scale(0.450001976353576,0.450001976353576) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ref.</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gen.</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">YourTTS</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">xTTSv2</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatinX (Fine-tuned)</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_rr ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatinX (DPO)</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ref.</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gen.</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">YourTTS</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">xTTSv2</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatinX (Fine-tuned)</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatinX (DPO)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="6"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">en</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">en</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">11.24</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">11.60</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">14.72</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8.52</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="6"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text">it</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">en</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">19.57</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">13.58</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">16.62</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.2.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10.71</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r">es</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">–</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">6.26</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">11.07</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_rr"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.08</span></td>
